EUCLIDEAN REGULAR TILING RECURSIONS
square self-recursion:
  lattice: Gaussian axis scaling m+0i
  indices m^2 for m=2..5: [4, 9, 16, 25]
  LRC role: self-dual square packet, scalar square counts are safe only
            when the chosen grid axes remain labelled.
triangle self-recursion:
  lattice: Eisenstein scaling m+0*omega
  general indices m^2 for m=2..5: [4, 9, 16, 25]
  binary chain emphasized by prompt: [4, 16, 64, 256]
  LRC role: triangular subdivision keeps orientation-sector labels;
            powers of 4 are the cleanest dyadic triangle spine.
triangle <-> hexagon dual bridge:
  local index: 6
  reason: a regular hexagon dissects into 6 equilateral triangles,
          and the triangular tiling has 6 triangles around a vertex.
  LRC role: support-six packet carrier, compatible with octahedral/current
            language but not a scalar replacement for q or C27 labels.
hexagon self-recursion:
  lattice: Eisenstein norm N(a+b*omega)=a^2-a*b+b^2
  N(3+omega)=7
  norm-7 powers: [7, 49, 343, 2401]
  centered-hex ring counts r=1..4: [7, 19, 37, 61]
  LRC role: the 7,49,... chain is a norm-index recursion;
            centered rings 7,19,37,... are a different carrier.

